Hi, 
	Is anybody familiar with Peter Neumann's (the same person who 
	moderates the RISKS mailing list) work on secure operating 
	systems in the late 1970's? Some people are saying 
	that the SCC patent is based on the same basic ideas
	first worked out by Neumann. I took a brief look 
	at one of his papers on citeseer: 
	
	http://citeseer.nj.nec.com/242537.html	

	but it appeared to be more about formally proving
	that an OS is secure than type enforcement. 

	David 
	




